# 26. Final Beta Definition

**PyFlare Beta is not a collection of unfinished features.**

It is a complete demonstration that PyFlare can function as a hardware-aware AI development environment.

The February 2027 beta must prove five fundamental ideas:

### 1. PyFlare understands context.

It can work with a real project rather than isolated prompts.

### 2. PyFlare routes deterministically.

Tasks are sent through explicit, inspectable execution paths.

### 3. PyFlare adapts to hardware.

AI configuration is selected according to the machine instead of assuming identical hardware.

### 4. PyFlare executes real work.

The system can interact with a real development environment, initially Unity.

### 5. PyFlare is a real product.

It can be installed, configured, authenticated, used and recovered from failures by an actual user.

